Stepping Through an Array
Once our data is in an array, we have new ways to “step through” all of the values, and operate on them one a time, without repeating code over and over.
We can do this using a “for” loop.
We can “declare” the index (we use “i” here) directly in the loop, because we only use/need it there.
i++ is a short way to say “increment i by 1”.   You can also use “i=i+1”.
Loops can run in reverse, too!
